      {
        "title": "engine/tests/pipeline/test_normalize.py",
        "content": "import pytest\nfrom pipeline.normalize import fold_name, normalize\n\ndef test_fold_name_not_yet_implemented():\n    with pytest.raises(NotImplementedError):\n        fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\")\n\n@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — pipeline/normalize.py::fold_name not implemented\")\nclass TestFoldName:\n    def test_strips_legal_suffix_from_tail(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\") == fold_name(\"Acme\")\n\n    def test_case_insensitive(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"ACME INC.\") == fold_name(\"acme inc\")\n\n    def test_suffix_as_substring_not_at_tail_is_not_stripped(self):\n        # \"Coco Inc Consulting\" — \"Inc\" is not the tail, must survive folding\n        assert \"inc\" in fold_name(\"Coco Inc Consulting\")\n\n    def test_multi_word_suffix_pvt_ltd(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\") == fold_name(\"Trellis Labs\")\n\n    def test_name_that_is_only_a_suffix_word_is_not_stripped_to_empty(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"LLC\") != \"\"\n\n    def test_empty_string_does_not_raise(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"\") == \"\"\n\n    def test_idempotent(self):\n        once = fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\")\n        assert fold_name(once) == once\n\n    def test_unicode_name(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Café GmbH\") != \"\"\n\n    def test_deterministic_for_same_input(self):\n        assert fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\") == fold_name(\"Acme Inc.\")\n\n\n@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Phase 2 — pipeline/normalize.py::normalize not implemented\")\nclass TestNormalize:\n    def test_empty_records_returns_empty_list(self):\n        assert normalize([], entity_type=\"account\", source_id=\"s1\") == []\n\n    def test_duplicate_external_ids_in_same_batch(self):\n        ...  # TODO: pin whether this raises, dedupes, or keeps both\n\n    def test_record_missing_expected_key_behavior(self):\n        ...  # TODO: pin whether this raises KeyError, ValidationError, or is skipped\n```\n\nApply this pattern to: `pipeline/blocking.py` (empty-side handling, `MIN_MATCH_CONFIDENCE=0.50` boundary inclusivity, duplicate `external_id` on one side), `pipeline/detect.py::classify`/`detect` (precedence ambiguity between structural/ownership/cosmetic when a value both folds-equal *and* is a structural field — flagged by the research agent as genuinely undefined in the current docstring, worth resolving with you before coding it), `agent/graph.py::select_rule`/`validate`/`resolve` (empty ruleset → universal escalation, tie-break-by-list-order semantics for equal-specificity rules), `db.py` (see §1d — this one is about an invariant, not just behavior), `eval/generate.py::generate` (**seed reproducibility is the single highest-value property test in this file** — `generate(seed=42,...) == generate(seed=42,...)` byte-for-byte), and `eval/harness.py` (division-by-zero in precision/recall when a manifest has zero conflicts — very likely first real bug once implemented).\n\n",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "1d. Missing error handling — gaps worth flagging even before implementation",
        "content": "\n| Where | Gap |\n|---|---|\n| `db.py` (all functions) | No test enforces the **table ownership invariant** from `AGENTS.md` — engine must never write `sources`/`rulesets`. Once implemented, this needs a test that spies on the DB connection/query log and asserts no INSERT/UPDATE ever targets those two tables, across every function in the module, not just the obvious ones. |\n| `main.py::execute_run` | Runs inside `BackgroundTasks`, which **silently swallows unhandled exceptions** in FastAPI. No test today would catch a background-task exception vanishing without `runs.status` ever reaching `\"failed\"`. This is a real production risk, not just a coverage gap — needs an explicit test once implemented that a raised exception inside `execute_run` results in `update_run_status(..., \"failed\", error=...)` being called, not a silent hang at `\"resolving\"`. |\n| `connectors/salesforce.py`, `connectors/warehouse.py` | Zero try/except anywhere; all `simple-salesforce`/DB-driver exceptions will propagate raw. `warehouse.py`'s `row_filter` is concatenated into a SQL string with no sanitization — worth a dedicated **SQL-injection-shaped-filter test**, not just a coverage note, once `extract` exists. |\n| `agent/graph.py::resolve` | No exception type exists for \"the model invented a value\" — `validate()` returning `False` is presumably converted to `escalated`, but nothing tests that a hallucinated `proposedValue` never reaches `auto_applied` even when `validate` is bypassed by a bug elsewhere (this is rule #2 in `AGENTS.md`'s three non-negotiables — deserves a dedicated adversarial test once the graph exists). |\n| `pipeline/detect.py::detect` | `entities: dict[UUID, CanonicalEntity]` lookup by `match.entity_a_id`/`entity_b_id` has no documented behavior for a missing key — will `KeyError` unguarded. Needs a characterization test either way. |\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "1e. Integration test gaps",
        "content": "\n```python\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "engine/tests/eval/test_harness_integration.py  (once Phase 2/3 land)",
        "content": "import pytest\nfrom eval.generate import generate, InjectionRates\nfrom eval.harness import run_system\n\n@pytest.mark.integration\nclass TestFullPipelineAgainstManifest:\n    def test_canon_full_beats_baseline_rules_on_synthetic_manifest(self, tmp_path):\n        \"\"\"The single most important test in the repo per AGENTS.md: canon_full\n        must outperform baseline_rules on the same generated manifest, or the\n        agent isn't earning its cost.\"\"\"\n        manifest = generate(seed=42, accounts=200, out_dir=tmp_path)\n        baseline = run_system(\"baseline_rules\", manifest, tmp_path)\n        full = run_system(\"canon_full\", manifest, tmp_path)\n        assert full.f1 >= baseline.f1\n        assert full.false_auto_apply_rate <= baseline.false_auto_apply_rate\n\n    def test_ambiguous_injections_are_escalated_not_guessed(self, tmp_path):\n        rates = InjectionRates(reparent=0, stale_attribute=0, name_variant=0,\n                                missing_record=0, duplicate_record=0, ambiguous=0.5)\n        manifest = generate(seed=1, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path, rates=rates)\n        metrics = run_system(\"canon_full\", manifest, tmp_path)\n        assert metrics.escalation_precision > 0.8  # genuinely ambiguous cases get escalated, not resolved\n\n    def test_validate_ablation_shows_invented_values_without_the_gate(self, tmp_path):\n        manifest = generate(seed=7, accounts=100, out_dir=tmp_path)\n        from eval.harness import ablate_without_validate\n        ablated = ablate_without_validate(manifest, tmp_path)\n        # Empirical proof the validate node matters — some invented-value rate > 0\n        assert ablated.false_auto_apply_rate > 0\n\n    def test_reproducible_generation_produces_identical_manifest(self, tmp_path):\n        m1 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"a\")\n        m2 = generate(seed=42, accounts=50, out_dir=tmp_path / \"b\")\n        assert m1 == m2\n```\n\nAlso missing: an **HTTP contract test** between `web/lib/server/engine.ts` and `engine/main.py` — a test that posts `{runId}` to a live/test-instance of the FastAPI app and asserts the response shape matches `engineStartRunResponseSchema` on the TypeScript side, since the two are hand-mirrored per `AGENTS.md`'s Tool Contract section and nothing currently enforces they stay in sync.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "Part 2 — `web/` (TypeScript / recommend vitest + testing-library)",
        "content": "\nThis is fully implemented, so these are gaps against *real, shippable* logic — highest priority.\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "2a. Untested pure functions (highest value — no mocking needed)",
        "content": "\n**`lib/validate-value.ts`** — this is the deterministic gate behind every override submission (`checkObservedValue`) and mirrors the engine's `validate` node in spirit. Business-critical, currently 0% covered.\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues, LEGAL_SUFFIXES } from \"./validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"is case-insensitive\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME INC\")).toBe(foldValue(\"acme inc\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips punctuation differences\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(foldValue(\"ACME INC\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips a single legal suffix\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Inc.\")).toBe(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips multiple legal suffixes iteratively (Pvt Ltd)\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not strip a name that is only a legal-suffix word\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).not.toBe(\"\");\n  });\n\n  it.each(LEGAL_SUFFIXES)(\"does not crash on suffix-only input: %s\", (suffix) => {\n    expect(() => foldValue(suffix)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"normalizes unicode (NFKD) before comparison\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Café GmbH\")).toBe(foldValue(\"Cafe GmbH\"));\n  });\n\n  it(\"collapses internal whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme   Corp\")).toBe(foldValue(\"Acme Corp\"));\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  const observed = [\"APAC-SOUTH\", \"APAC\"];\n\n  it(\"rejects an empty candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"\", observed).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"   \", observed).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"APAC-SOUTH\", observed);\n    expect(result).toMatchObject({ ok: true, matches: \"APAC-SOUTH\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts a folded/normalized match\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"apac south\", [\"APAC-SOUTH\"]);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a value matching neither side, exactly or folded\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"EMEA\", observed);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects when both observed sides are empty (orphan with nothing to compare)\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"anything\", []);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n    expect(result.reason).toMatch(/neither side/i);\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns the first matching real value when candidate folds-equal to multiple\", () => {\n    const result = checkObservedValue(\"acme\", [\"Acme Inc\", \"ACME\"]);\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"filters out empty-after-trim values from both sides\", () => {\n    const row = { sideA: { values: [\"  \", \"APAC\"] }, sideB: { values: [\"\"] } } as any;\n    expect(observedValues(row)).toEqual([\"APAC\"]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/diff-chars.ts`** — powers the diff-row character emphasis, the signature UI element per the design system.\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/diff-chars.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { diffSegments } from \"./diff-chars\";\n\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"returns whole value as prefix when strings are equal\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"finds a common prefix\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC-SOUTH\", \"APAC\")).toMatchObject({ prefix: \"APAC\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"finds a common suffix without overlapping the prefix\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"ACME-EAST\", \"ACME-WEST\");\n    expect(result.prefix).toBe(\"ACME-\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles completely disjoint strings (no shared prefix or suffix)\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"EMEA\", \"APAC\");\n    expect(result.prefix).toBe(\"\");\n    expect(result.suffix).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles one empty string\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"\", \"APAC\");\n    expect(result).toBeDefined();\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles one string being a prefix of the other\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC-SOUTH\");\n    expect(result.prefix).toBe(\"APAC\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not let prefix and suffix scans overlap on near-identical short strings\", () => {\n    const result = diffSegments(\"AB\", \"AC\");\n    expect(result.prefix.length + result.suffix.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(2);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/rule-trace.ts`** — a natural 4-case full-coverage table (the (ruleDecided × hasValue) matrix):\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/rule-trace.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { deriveRuleTrace } from \"./rule-trace\";\n\ndescribe(\"deriveRuleTrace\", () => {\n  it(\"returns a single unresolved step when there is no resolution yet\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace({ resolution: null } as any);\n    expect(trace).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect(trace[0].ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it.each([\n    [\"rule decided + value present (auto-apply path)\", true, true, { apply: true, propose: false }],\n    [\"rule decided + no value (escalate strategy)\", true, false, { apply: false, propose: false }],\n    [\"no rule + value present (model proposal path)\", false, true, { apply: false, propose: true }],\n    [\"no rule + no value (model also escalated)\", false, false, { apply: false, propose: false }],\n  ])(\"%s\", (_label, ruleDecided, hasValue, expected) => {\n    const row = {\n      resolution: {\n        appliedRuleId: ruleDecided ? \"r1\" : null,\n        proposedValue: hasValue ? \"APAC\" : \"\",\n      },\n    } as any;\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(row);\n    const byNode = Object.fromEntries(trace.map((s) => [s.node, s.ran]));\n    expect(byNode.classify).toBe(true);\n    expect(byNode.apply).toBe(expected.apply);\n    expect(byNode.propose).toBe(expected.propose);\n    expect(byNode.validate).toBe(hasValue);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/format.ts`** — boundary-heavy, deterministic, no excuse not to test:\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/format.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { formatElapsed, formatStat, formatRelative, formatConfidence } from \"./format\";\n\ndescribe(\"formatElapsed\", () => {\n  it(\"clamps negative durations to 0\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(-500)).toBe(formatElapsed(0));\n  });\n  it(\"formats sub-hour as mm:ss\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(65_000)).toBe(\"01:05\");\n  });\n  it(\"formats exactly one hour boundary with an hour prefix\", () => {\n    expect(formatElapsed(3_600_000)).toMatch(/^1h?:/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatStat\", () => {\n  it(\"distinguishes 0 (a real value) from null/undefined (not computed)\", () => {\n    expect(formatStat(0)).not.toBe(formatStat(null));\n    expect(formatStat(null)).toBe(formatStat(undefined));\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatRelative\", () => {\n  const now = new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:00:00Z\");\n  it(\"says 'just now' just under the 60s boundary\", () => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(now.getTime() - 59_000), now)).toMatch(/just now/i);\n  });\n  it(\"crosses into minutes at the 60s boundary\", () => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(now.getTime() - 60_000), now)).toMatch(/m ago/);\n  });\n  it(\"crosses into hours at the 60min boundary\", () => {\n    expect(formatRelative(new Date(now.getTime() - 3_600_000), now)).toMatch(/h ago/);\n  });\n  it(\"handles a future date without throwing or showing a negative count\", () => {\n    expect(() => formatRelative(new Date(now.getTime() + 5_000), now)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatConfidence\", () => {\n  it.each([[0, \"0.00\"], [1, \"1.00\"], [0.005, \"0.01\"]])(\"formats %s as %s\", (input, expected) => {\n    expect(formatConfidence(input)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/uuid.ts`**, **`lib/reviewer-label.ts`**, **`lib/audit-detail.ts`** — smaller but still zero-covered:\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/uuid.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { isUuid } from \"./uuid\";\n\ndescribe(\"isUuid\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts a well-formed v4 UUID\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"123e4567-e89b-42d3-a456-426614174000\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"is case-insensitive\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"123E4567-E89B-42D3-A456-426614174000\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it.each([\"banana\", \"\", \"123e4567-e89b-42d3-a456\", \"not-a-uuid-at-all-nope\"])(\n    \"rejects malformed input: %s\",\n    (input) => expect(isUuid(input)).toBe(false),\n  );\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/lib/reviewer-label.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewerLabel } from \"./reviewer-label\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"falls back through username -> email -> fallback id\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel(null, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n  it(\"uses username when present\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"vallabh\" } as any, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"vallabh\");\n  });\n  it(\"treats an empty-string username as present (?? only checks null/undefined)\", () => {\n    // Documents a real edge case: \"\" is not caught by `??`, so an empty username\n    // could produce an empty label rather than falling through to email/fallback.\n    const label = reviewerLabel({ username: \"\" } as any, \"user_123\");\n    expect(label).toBe(\"\"); // TODO: confirm this is intended, or switch to `||`\n  });\n});\n```\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "2b. Server-layer logic gaps (need a DB test double — Testcontainers/pg-mem, or dependency-inject the Drizzle client)",
        "content": "\n| Function | Gap | Test scenario |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lib/server/conflicts.ts::recordReview` | 4 distinct outcome codes (404/409×2/400/200) driven by nested state | Parametrized test hitting each branch: no target → 404; no resolution yet → 409; approve with empty proposed value → 409; override with invalid value → 400 (via `checkObservedValue`); happy path → 200 with correct audit `chosenValue` (null on reject, override value on override) |\n| `lib/server/export.ts::appliedValue` | Pure but untested; only 3 of many statuses count as \"applied\" | `it.each` over every `ResolutionStatus` value, asserting `null` for everything outside `{auto_applied, approved, overridden}` |\n| `lib/server/export.ts::applyDecisions` | \"Reparented\" flag is false when a decision sets parent back to its *original* value — subtle, easy to get backwards | Test explicitly: decision resolves parent to the account's current `parentExternalId` → `reparented: false`; resolves to a genuinely different value → `true` |\n| `lib/server/export.ts::decisionsToCsv`/`csvCell` | CSV escaping untested | `it.each` over values containing `\"`, `,`, `\\r\\n`, `null`, numbers — assert correct quoting/escaping and trailing `\\r\\n` |\n| `lib/server/rulesets.ts::createRulesetVersion` | Advisory-lock-based version numbering; race condition surface | Integration test: fire two concurrent `createRulesetVersion` calls for the *same* name against a real (or Testcontainers) Postgres, assert versions come out `1, 2` not `1, 1`; also test first-ever ruleset for a name gets version 1 |\n| `lib/server/runs.ts::failUndispatchedRun` | No-ops if run already progressed past `\"queued\"` (race with the engine) | Set a run to `\"matching\"`, call `failUndispatchedRun`, assert status is unchanged (not overwritten to `\"failed\"`) |\n| `lib/server/runs.ts::getSeverityBreakdown` | Silently drops out-of-range severity values instead of throwing | Insert a conflict row with severity `9` (simulating an engine bug) directly, assert it's dropped from the breakdown rather than crashing the page |\n| `lib/server/engine.ts::startRun` vs `fetchEngineStatus` | Deliberately asymmetric error contracts (one throws, one never does) — worth pinning explicitly | Mock `fetch` to reject: assert `startRun` throws `EngineUnreachableError`; assert `fetchEngineStatus` returns `null` instead |\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "2c. Missing error-handling tests (routes)",
        "content": "\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/runs/route.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\n// mock lib/server/* and lib/server/engine per your DI approach\n\ndescribe(\"POST /api/runs\", () => {\n  it(\"400s when sourceAId equals sourceBId\", async () => {\n    // both same uuid → expect 400 \"must be different systems\"\n  });\n\n  it(\"400s when sourceA no longer exists\", async () => {\n    // findSourceIds mocked to omit sourceAId\n  });\n\n  it(\"400s when the ruleset version no longer exists\", async () => {\n    // getRuleset mocked to return null\n  });\n\n  it(\"still returns 201 with the created run when the engine is unreachable\", async () => {\n    // startRun mocked to throw EngineUnreachableError\n    // assert: 201, runId present, failUndispatchedRun called, run_failed audit appended\n    // this is a deliberate design choice per AGENTS.md — pin it so it can't regress silently\n  });\n\n  it(\"rethrows and 500s on a non-EngineUnreachableError failure from startRun\", async () => {\n    // startRun mocked to throw a plain Error\n  });\n\n  it(\"400s on malformed JSON body\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"PATCH /api/conflicts/:conflictId/resolution\", () => {\n  it(\"404s for a non-UUID conflictId before even parsing the body\", async () => {});\n  it(\"400s when action=override is missing overrideValue\", async () => {});\n  it(\"propagates recordReview's status code and message verbatim (404/409/400)\", async () => {});\n  it(\"200s with reviewedBy from the authenticated reviewer, not the request body\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/runs/[runId]/export/route.test.ts\ndescribe(\"GET /api/runs/:runId/export\", () => {\n  it(\"400s on an empty sections query string\", async () => {});      // ?sections=\n  it(\"dedupes and reorders sections to canonical order regardless of input order\", async () => {\n    // ?sections=hierarchy,stats should produce identical output to ?sections=stats,hierarchy\n  });\n  it(\"400s on an unknown section name\", async () => {});\n  it(\"400s on an unrecognized format\", async () => {});               // ?format=xml\n  it(\"validates format/sections/run-existence BEFORE the auth check\", async () => {\n    // documents current ordering — worth a deliberate decision, not an accident\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// web/app/api/_lib/respond.test.ts\ndescribe(\"parseJson\", () => {\n  it(\"400s on malformed JSON body\", async () => {});\n  it(\"400s on valid JSON that fails schema validation, with ALL issues (not just the first)\", async () => {});\n  it(\"maps nested/array paths to dot-joined keys, including numeric array indices\", async () => {\n    // e.g. rules[0].preferredSourceId\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to '_' key for schema-level refine errors with an empty path\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\nAlso worth a dedicated test on `lib/api-client.ts::postJson`/`patchJson`: a 2xx response with an unparseable JSON body currently returns `{ok: true, data: null}` — a **silently wrong-typed success**, not an error. That's a real footgun worth a named test (`\"returns ok:true with null data when a 2xx response has an unparseable body\"`) so it's a documented behavior, not an accident someone trips over later.\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "2d. Integration test gaps (Playwright / testing-library)",
        "content": "\nNone of these can be caught by unit tests — they cross the DB, the engine boundary, or actual rendered UI:\n\n1. **Full review flow, end to end**: seed a run with an escalated conflict → load `/conflicts` → approve/reject/override via the UI → assert the queue row updates, the audit trail gets a new entry, and (for override) the value shown matches the normalized `matches` value, not the raw typed input.\n2. **Keyboard-only queue navigation** — `AGENTS.md`'s design system explicitly requires `j`/`k`/`a`/`e`/`o` to work without a mouse for a 400-row queue. This is a hard requirement with zero test coverage today.\n3. **Run creation → engine unreachable → still-201 UX**: start a run against a stubbed/down engine, assert the UI still shows the run (as `failed`) rather than erroring the whole page — this exercises the deliberate `route.ts` behavior in §2c live.\n4. **Rulesets are versioned, never mutated**: create a ruleset, run a reconciliation against it, create a new version with the same name, and assert the original run's `rulesetId` still resolves to the *old* version's rules (reproducibility contract from `AGENTS.md`).\n5. **Concurrent double-submit on `use-review.ts`**: fire two `submit()` calls for different conflicts in quick succession from a test, assert `pendingId` reflects the most recent call and doesn't get stuck on a stale value if the earlier call resolves later.\n6. **CSV/JSON export round-trip**: export a run with known seeded data via both `?format=csv` and `?format=json`, assert row counts and values match between formats and match the DB directly.\n7. **Auth boundary**: every route handler calls `requireReviewer()`, but ordering varies (some check UUID/body shape first, some check auth first — see §2c export route note). A single parametrized Playwright/supertest suite hitting every route unauthenticated should assert each one refuses correctly, since a manual per-route check is exactly where one gets missed.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Priority order if you want to tackle this incrementally",
